  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive ({他動詞|たどうし}). Pattern: 〜を{描|か}く.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {絵|え}を{描|か}く: draw a picture\n- {地図|ちず}を{描|か}く: draw a map\n- {眉|まゆ}を{描|か}く: draw on eyebrows (with makeup)\n- {漫画|まんが}を{描|か}く: draw manga\n\nPRONUNCIATION:\n{描|か}く and {描|えが}く are the same verb in dictionary terms but differ in nuance:\n- {描|か}く (kaku): everyday, concrete acts of drawing (pictures, lines, makeup)\n- {描|えが}く: more literary or abstract — depicting, portraying, envisioning\n\nDO NOT CONFUSE WITH:\n- {書|か}く: to write — same reading, different kanji; used for letters, characters, text\n- {掻|か}く: to scratch — same reading; used for scratching the body, perspiring, etc.",
